# The Pixhawk settings the companion stack relies on, for the team airframe.
# Load in Mission Planner (Config > Full Parameter List > Load from file)
# AFTER aerothon_failsafe.parm, then reboot. Copter 4.5.
#
# Without these the stack's MAVLink commands are accepted and do nothing:
# camera_ctrl's MAV_CMD_DO_MOUNT_CONTROL needs a mount, winch_ctrl's
# MAV_CMD_DO_WINCH needs a winch, and MAVROS needs the port it is wired to.
#
# CHANNELS ARE WIRING. SERVO9 (AUX1) for the tilt servo and SERVO10 (AUX2) for
# the winch are a guess at the build: set the SERVOn lines to the outputs the
# servo and the winch ESC are actually on, and put the old function back on
# any output these would take over.

# Companion link: Pi 5 UART on TELEM2 at 921600 baud, MAVLink 2
# (mission2.launch.py fcu_url:=/dev/ttyAMA0:921600).
SERIAL2_PROTOCOL 2
SERIAL2_BAUD 921

# Camera tilt: a hobby servo as mount 1, pitch only, commanded over MAVLink.
# The stack's poses run from -90 (NADIR) to 0 (FORWARD); the joint allows +30.
MNT1_TYPE 1
MNT1_PITCH_MIN -90
MNT1_PITCH_MAX 30
MNT1_DEFLT_MODE 2
SERVO9_FUNCTION 7
# Calibrate SERVO9_MIN / SERVO9_MAX so the commanded angles are the real
# ones: command NADIR and FORWARD from the GCS and check with a protractor
# (docs/FIELD_READINESS.md, bench check 5).

# Winch: PWM-driven, no encoder; length is integrated from the commanded
# rate, which winch_ctrl already assumes (payout_rate_mps).
WNCH_TYPE 1
WNCH_RATE_MAX 1.0
SERVO10_FUNCTION 88
